  "id": "COMPOUND:22367 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Oncostemonol B and CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of target interactions. Oncostemonol B is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Astragaloside a em leader pound, Voacamine, and (R)-Pabulenol, all of which are implicated in targeting CCRF-HSB-2. These findings indicate that Oncostemonol B may act as a mediator in the signaling pathways leading to the activation of CCRF-HSB-2. The varying scores across the three paths suggest that the strength of the interaction may differ, but all pathways consistently link Oncostemonol B to CCRF-HSB-2 through intermediate targets. The evidence supports a possible role for Oncostemonol B in modulating the activity of these compounds, which in turn influence CCRF-HSB-2. The mechanisms underlying this relationship are not fully elucidated, and further research is needed to determine the precise biological pathways involved.",
